                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a3dab3b6-5305-37c0-a84d-06a0f16e054d",
                        "entry_id": "babb488a-9bc5-3d4d-aab9-4e01946fc540",
                        "glosses": [
                            "self-dwarfing"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3844bd50-4b54-4eb9-aad0-43a0c7ea40b0",
                                "sense_id": "a3dab3b6-5305-37c0-a84d-06a0f16e054d",
                                "text": "Es gibt ein Sprichwort bei den Chinesen, das die Mütter schon ihre Kinder lehren: siao-sin »mache dein Herz klein!« Dies ist der eigentliche Grundhang in späten Zivilisationen: ich zweifle nicht, daß ein antiker Grieche auch an uns Europäern von heute zuerst die Selbstverkleinerung herauserkennen würde – damit allein schon gingen wir ihm »wider den Geschmack«.",
                                "translation": "The Chinese have a proverb which mothers even teach their children: \"Siao-sin\" (\"make thy heart small\"). This is the essentially fundamental tendency in latter-day civilisations. I have no doubt that an ancient Greek, also, would first of all remark the self-dwarfing in us Europeans of to-day--in this respect alone we should immediately be \"distasteful\" to him.",
                                "english": "The Chinese have a proverb which mothers even teach their children: \"Siao-sin\" (\"make thy heart small\"). This is the essentially fundamental tendency in latter-day civilisations. I have no doubt that an ancient Greek, also, would first of all remark the self-dwarfing in us Europeans of to-day--in this respect alone we should immediately be \"distasteful\" to him."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
